<newsitem itemid="222415" id="root" date="1996-11-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Laser slumps to yr loss, no div.</title>
<headline>Laser slumps to yr loss, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		27.5 loss   vs 15.2 loss</p>
<p>    - attrib		  18.6 loss   vs 0.1 profit</p>
<p>    After tax		 3.35 loss   vs 0.02 profit</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   9.60 loss   vs 0.32 loss</p>
<p>    Tax credit		6.26	  vs 0.34</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   20.79	 vs 18.13</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     5.27 loss   vs 2.20 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		  263.59	vs 263.38</p>
<p>Full name: Laser Transport Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said Laser's two divisions were currently trading profitably. They anticipated that unless economic conditions deteriorated dramatically, both would achieve satisfactory profit levels in the 1997 year.</p>
<p>The board was confident of resuming dividend payments next year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
